                <pb facs="0382" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg334"/>

                <head>No. 182.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Count Litta to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Italy in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1877-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 15, 1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    inform your excellency that the Government of His Majesty the King, my august
                    sovereign, has instructed me to give notice of its desire for the termination of
                    the consular convention concluded between Italy and the United States February
                    8, 1868, availing itself of the privilege granted to the parties who signed it
                    by article 17 of said convention. My government advises me that a similar
                    communication has been made to the legation of the United States at Borne.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion to renew, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>LITTA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
